            "frame_00206.png",
            "frame_00207.png",
            "frame_00208.png",
            "frame_00209.png",
            "frame_00210.png",
            "frame_00211.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Remember, everything around you your hand, your table, this board, the wall, the ceiling, anything, your pen, it's all made of atoms."
    },
    {
        "id": 60,
        "start": 346.88,
        "end": 348.64,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00212.png",
            "frame_00213.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "And what are atoms made of?"
    },
    {
        "id": 61,
        "start": 348.64,
        "end": 357.44,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00214.png",
            "frame_00215.png",
            "frame_00216.png",
            "frame_00217.png",
            "frame_00218.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Tiny particles, and these particles have different properties like mass, charge, magnetic properties, etc."
    },
    {
        "id": 62,
        "start": 357.44,
        "end": 360.88,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00219.png",
            "frame_00220.png",
            "frame_00221.png",
            "frame_00222.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Here we are worried only about the electrical properties."
    },
    {
        "id": 63,
        "start": 360.88,
        "end": 367.36,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00223.png",
            "frame_00224.png",
            "frame_00225.png",
            "frame_00226.png",
            "frame_00227.png",
            "frame_00228.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Long, long time back, people used to wonder why things attract or repel each other."
    },
    {
        "id": 64,
        "start": 367.36,
        "end": 375.36,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00229.png",
            "frame_00230.png",
            "frame_00231.png",
            "frame_00232.png",
            "frame_00233.png",
            "frame_00234.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "For example, you take a comb and you comb your hair, and then you see that it attracts bits and pieces of paper."
    },
    {
        "id": 65,
        "start": 375.36,
        "end": 386.56,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00235.png",
            "frame_00236.png",
            "frame_00237.png",
            "frame_00238.png",
            "frame_00239.png",
            "frame_00240.png",
            "frame_00241.png",
            "frame_00242.png",
            "frame_00243.png",
            "frame_00244.png",
            "frame_00245.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Or when you rub a rod on some woolen or silk cloth, then it seemed that the rod or that cloth repels or attracts some other objects."
    },
    {
        "id": 66,
        "start": 386.56,
        "end": 398.48,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00246.png",
            "frame_00247.png",
            "frame_00248.png",
            "frame_00249.png",
            "frame_00250.png",
            "frame_00251.png",
            "frame_00252.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "So people used to wonder, and later on in the last 200-300 years, it was understood that these are basically due to charges, and there are two kinds of charges."
    },
    {
        "id": 67,
        "start": 398.48,
        "end": 404.56,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00253.png",
            "frame_00254.png",
            "frame_00255.png",
            "frame_00256.png",
            "frame_00257.png",
            "frame_00258.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "Actually, there is a third type as well, but that is something called as a neutral charge or no charge."
    },
    {
        "id": 68,
        "start": 404.56,
        "end": 409.44,
        "frames": [
            "frame_00259.png",
            "frame_00260.png",
            "frame_00261.png",
            "frame_00262.png",
            "frame_00263.png"
        ],
        "transcript": "So an atom is made up of three kinds of things, alright."
    },
    {
        "id": 69,
        "start": 409.44,
        "end": 414.8,
        "frames": [
